# CQ 16: Which signals carry which information parameters?
#
# Entry 351-42-24 defines the signal as a physical variable of which one or
# more parameters carry information about one or more variables. The
# information parameter, 351-42-25, is that parameter.
#
# The distinction is what separates the carrier from what is carried: the same
# current carries a temperature or a position depending on what its magnitude
# is taken to mean, and a model that states only the current has not said what
# it is a signal of.
#
# Empty on the three cases, which describe their chains in terms of variables
# rather than of the signals conveying them. That is the level Figures 1 and 2
# work at, and the question is here for a model that goes below it.
PREFIX iec60050: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#>
SELECT ?signal ?informationParameter
WHERE {
  ?signal a iec60050:Signal .
  OPTIONAL { ?signal iec60050:carriesInformationParameter ?informationParameter }
} ORDER BY ?signal
